      },
      "edits": [
        {
          "mode": "insert_after",
          "anchor": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The version I entered was called <strong>Chapter Three</strong>, a maze-like haunted-house experience where you choose your own path. Outside it was all cute statues and cheerful trains. In here, the mood was quite different.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
          "fragment": "<!-- tsurikue-en-photo-warehouse-20261113 -->\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":4150,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"https://tsurikue.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/tsurikue-sakaiminato-4138-08.jpg\" alt=\"Ticket price board at the entrance to Kitaro Yokai Warehouse\" class=\"wp-image-4150\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The admission board outside the warehouse when I visited.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->"
        },
        {
          "mode": "insert_after",
          "anchor": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The ticket doubled as a special <em>lucky charm sheet</em>. The idea was to collect five stamps, choosing four of the blessings yourself—things like good financial luck and road safety—then completing the final mark.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
          "fragment": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":4151,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"https://tsurikue.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/tsurikue-sakaiminato-4138-09.jpg\" alt=\"Ticket and lucky-charm stamp sheet from Kitaro Yokai Warehouse\" class=\"wp-image-4151\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Even the ticket becomes part of the adventure.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":4152,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"https://tsurikue.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/tsurikue-sakaiminato-4138-10.jpg\" alt=\"Yokai Warehouse stamp-collecting mission instructions\" class=\"wp-image-4152\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The stamp mission begins. I'll leave the final location a surprise.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->"
        },
        {
          "mode": "insert_after",
          "anchor": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The route brought me into a strange mirror-filled area. Next came the familiar flat-faced yokai <strong>Nurikabe</strong>. That expression is hard to dislike.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
          "fragment": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":4153,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"https://tsurikue.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/tsurikue-sakaiminato-4138-11.jpg\" alt=\"Mirror-filled area inside Kitaro Yokai Warehouse\" class=\"wp-image-4153\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The first mirror-filled room.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":4154,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"https://tsurikue.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/tsurikue-sakaiminato-4138-12.jpg\" alt=\"Nurikabe yokai figure inside Kitaro Yokai Warehouse\" class=\"wp-image-4154\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Nurikabe, with that unmistakable expression.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->"
        },
        {
          "mode": "insert_after",
          "anchor": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>But deeper inside, the colors and lighting made things less welcoming. Then there was <strong>Neko Musume</strong>—a character I'd always thought I knew. Under those lights, she looked unexpectedly frightening.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
          "fragment": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":4155,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"https://tsurikue.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/tsurikue-sakaiminato-4138-13.jpg\" alt=\"Yokai figure under eerie purple lighting inside Kitaro Yokai Warehouse\" class=\"wp-image-4155\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">The lighting changes everything.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:image {\"id\":4156,\"sizeSlug\":\"full\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img src=\"https://tsurikue.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/tsurikue-sakaiminato-4138-14.jpg\" alt=\"Kitaro and Neko Musume illuminated by green light in Yokai Warehouse\" class=\"wp-image-4156\"/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">A familiar pair, suddenly looking much creepier.</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->"
        },
        {
          "mode": "replace",
          "anchor": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Photography note:</strong> The attraction's current official rules ask visitors not to take photos or record video inside. The English article therefore doesn't reproduce my older indoor photos; please follow the rules in effect during your visit.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
          "fragment": "<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>About these photos:</strong> I received permission at the venue to publish these still photos on my blog. Video was not allowed, and I deliberately left out the scenes that would spoil the surprises. Please follow the staff's current photography guidance during your own visit.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
